# Line endings the scripts actually need, rather than whatever the checkout
# platform defaults to.
#
# A .sh file checked out with CRLF fails on Linux as "bad interpreter: No such
# file or directory", which names the interpreter and not the real problem. A
# .cmd file wants CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses the last line of an LF-only batch
# file, and reports the error against something else entirely.
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
